============================================================================================
ANCILLA FAN-OUT — trading qubits and gates for depth
============================================================================================
  One controlled Trotter step of H_sense, terms layer-sorted in both arms.
  serial = every term controlled on one ancilla; fanout = one copy per
  term within a layer, CNOT tree in and out.

     N  layers   F  depth serial  depth fanout  speedup  cx serial  cx fanout  unitary err
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     4       6   2            57            54      1.1         36         38     0.00e+00
     6       6   3            60            55      1.1         60         64     0.00e+00
     8       6   4            69            55      1.3         84         90     0.00e+00
    10       6   5            87            56      1.6        108        116          nan
    12       6   6           105            56      1.9        132        142          nan

  depth  serial N^0.55   fanout N^0.03
  cx     serial N^1.18   fanout N^1.20

  A fanout depth exponent near 0 means V3's duration can be held under
  rep_delay at every N, and its 3 circuits/epoch then beat V4's 5 outright.
  But read the cx columns first: if fan-out RAISES gate count, it makes
  V3's fidelity problem worse while fixing a cost problem that sorting had
  already mostly solved - a bad trade for the thing V3 actually needs.
